//! flags: -b llvm --triple x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --mcpu generic

// How the maths reaches the target when there is no vector math library.
//
// LLVM has intrinsics for the hyperbolic functions and, since LLVM 19, for
// asin, acos and atan, but not for atanh: so `cosh` and `asin` become
// llvm.cosh and llvm.asin, which on a scalar are legalised into the calls to
// libm's coshf and asinf a C compiler emits for std::cosh and std::asin -- the
// same function, and so the same answer bit for bit -- and `atanh` is that
// call to atanhf directly. Bit for bit matters: apps/pbrt rounds a wavelength
// to the nearest nanometre before indexing a table, and a last-bit difference
// in atanh occasionally picks the neighbouring entry.
//
// The vector case is the one worth pinning, and it is pinned to a generic
// machine on purpose. libm is scalar, so on a machine with no vector math
// library a vector `atanh` has to be taken a lane at a time -- four
// extractelements, four calls and four insertelements below -- where `cosh`
// and `asin` stay single vector intrinsics that LLVM legalises into the same
// shape further down. Following the host instead, the compiler asks the
// host's libmvec what it has and lowers all three to one call of its vector
// entry point (`_ZGVbN4v_atanhf`, see CodeGen_LLVM::probe_host_vector_math),
// which is what apps/pbrt's gangs get; that output depends on the machine
// and is not what a golden can hold. Getting either wrong is not a miscompile
// that shows up as a wrong number; it is one that fails to build.
func [[export]]scalar_atanh(x : f32) -> f32 = atanh(x);
func [[export]]scalar_cosh(x : f32) -> f32 = cosh(x);
// It is what AngleBetween in the mesh-light sampling rests on.
func [[export]]scalar_asin(x : f32) -> f32 = asin(x);

func [[export]]vector_atanh(v : vector[f32, 4]) -> vector[f32, 4] = atanh(v);
func [[export]]vector_cosh(v : vector[f32, 4]) -> vector[f32, 4] = cosh(v);
func [[export]]vector_asin(v : vector[f32, 4]) -> vector[f32, 4] = asin(v);

// Double precision goes to the unsuffixed entry point, as C's overloads do.
func [[export]]double_atanh(x : f64) -> f64 = atanh(x);
